  complianceInfo="All new residential and commercial plumbing installations in Queensland must be completed by a QBCC-licensed plumber and drainer. A Certificate of Compliance (Form 9) is required for all notifiable work and must be provided to the building owner before practical completion. Plumbing must comply with the Queensland Plumbing and Drainage Act 2018, AS/NZS 3500 and the National Construction Code (NCC). Pulse Plumbing provides all required documentation for council inspections, QBCC audits and practical completion handover packs."
  faqs={[
    {
      q: 'What stages of a new build do you cover?',
      a: 'We cover all stages: underground drainage and sewer connections before slab pour, rough-in during frame stage (water supply, drainage, gas), and fit-off after internal linings (fixtures, appliances, hot water system). We also complete pressure tests and liaise with council inspectors.',
    },
    {
      q: 'How do you coordinate with the builder and other trades?',
      a: 'We work directly with the site supervisor and project manager, communicating any scheduling changes promptly. We understand that plumbing delays cascade to other trades — our scheduling systems are built around keeping your program on track.',
    },
    {
      q: 'Do you provide Form 9 certificates for new builds?',
      a: 'Yes. A Form 9 (Certificate of Compliance) is issued for all notifiable plumbing work. We also provide pressure test records, soil report documentation and any other compliance paperwork required for council inspections or practical completion.',
